  "methodology": "36 claim-level cases built from real Phase-5 Evidence (via evidence/adapters.py against real captured raw records, reused from the Phase-5/Phase-6 Evidence pool). Two complementary categories per contract Step 8: natural claims paraphrasing real Evidence content, and controlled deterministic mutations (wrong numeral, wrong entity, added unsupported qualifier, negated fact) with independently-authored, pre-frozen gold. Gold labels authored BEFORE any evaluator candidate ran, from direct inspection of the real Evidence content (never from candidate output).",
  "scale_caveat": "36 cases is smaller than the suggested 60-case target - a first Phase-7 benchmark, not claimed as equivalent statistical power. The real-Evidence pool available in this session (reused from Phase-5/6's already-captured records) supported this scale cleanly; documented honestly rather than padding with lower-quality synthetic cases.",
